    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1230">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1042"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/365</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Parker, representing American
                        interests</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-17T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 17, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>669. Reported Mexico City papers, on 12th instant, contained statement that
                    mining decree of September 14 would not be enforced until May 14.</p>
                <p>Investigate and telegraph whether this correct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
